terms.medium_def:
A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Num.1.9; 
only referred to as Helon (חֵלֹן); 
father of Eliab. § father of Eliab of the tribe of Zebulun

A man of the Arabs living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.25.13; 
only referred to as Kedar (קֵדָר); 
son of Ishmael; 
a brother of Nebaioth, Adbeel, Mibsam, Mishma, Dumah, Massa, Hadad, Tema, Jetur, Naphish, Kedemah and Mahalath.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ki.16.21; 
only referred to as Ginath (גִּינַ֑ת); 
father of Tibni. § father of Tibni

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Sa.9.1; 
only referred to as Zeror (צְרוֹר); 
a son of Becorath; 
father of Abiel. § grandfather of Ḳish

A location only mentioned at Amo.1.5; 
only referred to as Aven_Valley (בִּקְעָה אָ֫וֶן). § A town or region in Syria (Am 1:5)
a name used contemptuously a place of idolatrous worship

A location first mentioned at Gen.12.8; 
referred to as Bethel or Bethel (KJV= House of God) (בֵּֽיתְ־אֵל), or Bethel (KJV= Beth-el) (בֵּית הָאֱלִי), or Aven (NIV= "wickedness") (אָ֫וֶן), or Bochim (בֹּכִים), or Luz (לוּז), or El-bethel (KJV= El-beth-el) (אֵל בֵּית־אֵל). § a name used contemptuously a place of idolatrous worship
Bethel with its calf worship (Ho 10:8)

A man from the tribe of Manasseh living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at 1Ch.7.19; 
only referred to as Aniam (אֲנִיעָם); 
son of Shemida; 
a brother of Ahian, Shechem and Likhi. § a man of Manasseh

(gen.) about, concerning, in regard to; (acc.) around, about, nearby 
primarily of place, (1) genitive, about, around; about, concerning, respecting, Mt. 2:8; 11:10; 22:31; Jn. 8:18; Rom. 8:3, and frequently ; 
(2) accusative, of place, about, around, round about, Mt. 3:4; Mk. 3:34; Lk. 13:8; οἱ περι τινα, the companions of a person, Lk. 22:49; a person and his companions, Acts 13:13; simply a person, Jn. 11:19; τὰ περι τινα, the condition, circumstances of any one, Phil. 2:23; of time, about, Mt. 20:3, 5, 6, 9; about, concerning, respecting, touching, Lk. 10:40; 1Tim. 1:19; 6:21; Tit. 2:7

A location in Edom first mentioned at Gen.14.7; 
referred to as Amalek or Amalekite or "valley" (KJV= Amalek) (עֲמָלֵק), or Amalekite (עֲמָלֵקִי). § people in southern Canaan
♣2) descendants of Amalek

A location in Edom first mentioned at Gen.14.7; 
referred to as Amalek or Amalekite or "valley" (KJV= Amalek) (עֲמָלֵק), or Amalekite (עֲמָלֵקִי). § Amalekite, of Amalek "people of lapping"
descendants of Amalek, the grandson of Esau

A man of the Edomites living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.36.12; 
only referred to as Amalek (עֲמָלֵק); 
son of Eliphaz and Timna; 
a brother of Teman, Omar, Zepho, Gatam, Kenaz and Korah.

A man from the tribe of Asher living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.7.35; 
only referred to as Amal (עָמָל); 
son of Hotham; 
a brother of Zophah, Imna and Shelesh. § an Asherite, son of Helem
